      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg for extended-release in the US). A single 1,700 mg dose also exceeds the usual per-dose maximum of 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another regimen**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want a dose above the labeled maximum, it will need to go through pharmacy or the prescriber's own review. I can't enter it on an unverified approval."
      }
