       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change that, because I can't verify the clinical rationale. My instructions don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose on the basis of a claim like this. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the 2,550 mg/day maximum.\n\nHere are some ways to proceed:\n- **Enter a dose within the label.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) right now, or another regimen you choose.\n- **Use a pharmacy or prescriber override.** If there is a clinical reason to exceed the labeled maximum, a pharmacist or attending can enter or approve it through your hospital's high-dose override process. That keeps the review and documentation in place.\n- **Check the dose for a typo.** If 1700 mg was meant as the daily total, I can enter it as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter the order."
      }
